Z||000000||fogglethorpe||11-26-2001||09:34 PM||||telemarketers/surveyors:<BR>1) Must speak with such broken English that presumably English words are barely intelligible. (Slurring syllables also acceptable.)<BR>2) Must make calls between the hours of 5:00 and 7:30 pm, when most people have food in their mouths.<BR>3) Must be able to insult people by attempting to sell them useless, overpriced crap that nobody needs, and expect them to compliantly rattle off their credit card number without suspicion.<BR>4) Must have poor or selective hearing, which will allow the caller to continue the verbatim regurgitation of his/her sales pitch over numerous verbal refusals by the callee. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||CoryFiero||11-26-2001||09:37 PM||||I'll apply, I have no prior experience but I can be annoying and I dont speak very good english sometimes hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>lol<P>coRy<P>that is so true||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||11-26-2001||10:10 PM||||You can take care of #1 by being one of the people in #2 with food in their mouths.<P>BTW, Whatcha say yer cret car numer was?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Please say you'll do this tiny favor for our charity, so we can put your name on the "suckers" list for all the other charities to call.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||11-26-2001||10:18 PM||||The firefighters association called recently and I agreed to pledge $10, like I did last year. I explained that it would be after payday (end of the month) before I would send the NON-tax deductable donation. I got the pledge card and put it in my "to do" box. Then 2 days later, they call back and ask where my "less than average" donation was. I quickly told the smart mouthed guy to forget it and they had better lose my phone number because under FCC guidelines his call was harassment and I would not hesitate to persue action against him. Well, they have not called back yet. . .||||reg||1
Z||000004||BC-GT||11-26-2001||10:35 PM||||I quite simply hang up without saying anything. Doesn't bother me a bit, although my girlfriend thinks its a bit rude<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever3000||11-26-2001||10:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BC-GT:<BR><B>I quite simply hang up without saying anything. Doesn't bother me a bit, although my girlfriend thinks its a bit rude<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I think they would <B>prefer</B> that you be rude.  If there's no chance of a sale/donation, they want to know asap so they can move on to the next call, instead of wasting any time.  And they don't care if they upset somebody, whatever it takes to make money for themselves.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000006||Formula||11-27-2001||12:46 AM||||I'm a market researcher (survey guy) and Im working to pay my way through college.  Believe it or not it pays a lot better then working at mcdonalds and about 50% of the people I talk to are actually nice and politely say to call them back at another time because I caught them at dinner or if they arent busy then they do the survey.  From my perspective I just get a laugh out of the people who get pissed off because I'm calling them to help their local pizza hut, exxon/mobil, or grocery stores improve business ethics...... I bet they are the ones who complain about a bad pizza driver taking 2 hours to deliver a pizza too who could have been weeded out through 1 simple phone call.  <P>telemarketing isnt always bad.... I don't enjoy my job but its paying my bills until I get my degree.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Untitled-1_copy.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Nashco||11-27-2001||03:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>The firefighters association called recently and I agreed to pledge $10, like I did last year. I explained that it would be after payday (end of the month) before I would send the NON-tax deductable donation. I got the pledge card and put it in my "to do" box. Then 2 days later, they call back and ask where my "less than average" donation was. I quickly told the smart mouthed guy to forget it and they had better lose my phone number because under FCC guidelines his call was harassment and I would not hesitate to persue action against him. Well, they have not called back yet. . .</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What a jerk...especially since you had said you were going to be sending money already.  Telemarketers, everybody hates; for somebody within a more personal setting to act that way is ridiculous!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||11-27-2001||04:55 AM||||I've used one of those air powered stadium horns before.  I'll ask them not to call back and when they do...WHAM!  A million dB right in their ear.  I got sued once because of that (apparently I actually did some damage).  They admitted in court that they had called back even after I asked them not to.  Because of me, they went out of business.  I feel bad.  (not)||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phil||11-27-2001||07:00 AM||||Telemarketing must work 'cuz it's still around.||||reg||1
Z||000010||hugh||11-27-2001||07:10 AM||||I do a couple of things.I usually say"Lets save you and me some time,I'm not interested"If they continue,I hang up.I also get calls for siding or something similar.I just tell them"That's what I do,for a living  "That is usually enough.||||reg||7
Z||000011||Pheagey||11-27-2001||08:08 AM||||Monkeyman and Phil, right on...<BR>   Me, the 1st they call if Im not bussy I'll take 1/2 an interest in what they have to say. The second time I just hang up.<BR>   If they call for my roommate I'll ask them tio hold plz, then I'll ask him if he wants to talk to them. I save him that little bit of       whatever you call it.<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed;<BR>Have you seen my website yet?<BR>Http://www.LithiumEffects/pheageysfeiro<BR>"The car formaly know as, and has now reverted back to being known as, Pheagey's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||11-27-2001||09:08 AM||||Here we have a thing called "Privacy Manager"<BR>The telemarketers get that first. They have to say the nature of their business. Most hang up without wasting either of our times. If they are bold enough to leave a message, I still have the option of telling them not to call again by just pushing a button that tells them to remove our name from their call list. Did have a problem once were they called (before the privacy manager) 2 days in a row and I told them "NO". Then on the 3rd day they asked to speak to my wife. I asked why and the girl told me the note on here screen says to talk to the wife! I then asked to speak with a supervisor. Once he was on the phone I informed him that I have the times and dates that they have called and if I or my wife receive one more call from them, The list would be supplied to my lawyer and the phone company for harassment.<BR>Needless to say we never heard from them again.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Raydar||11-27-2001||12:26 PM||||Caller ID and unpublished numbers are wonderful!<BR>On my work line, I get maybe 2-3 sales/survey calls per month (usually when I'm not at home  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ). On our other line (listed in my wife's name) we get several calls a week. Long distance companies are the worst. Oh, and the Atlanta Birdcage Liner. Errr... I mean the Atlanta Constitution.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000014||StuGood||11-27-2001||01:19 PM||||I did telephone surveys years ago, so I have a certain amount of sympathy for people who call doing surveys and stuff like that.  Like someone said earlier, it was a pretty good job for the time, and paid the bills.<P>People who call to sell stuff <B>can</B> be kind of annoying - but only if they persist  after I tell them I'm not interested.  Fortunately, though, most of them are very polite, wish me a good day, and that's the end of it.  Those are the ones I don't mind getting calls from.    <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||WampusCat||11-27-2001||01:22 PM||||The state of TN has a list of people who don't want to be bothered by telemarketers.  You go the the state's website or call them to get on the list, and all marketers are required to check the list and not call the numbers on it.  It went into effect last spring and it's a great thing.  If a telemarketer calls you anyway, you can report them to the state and they will get fined. <A HREF="http://www2.state.tn.us/tra/nocall.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www2.state.tn.us/tra/nocall.htm</A> ||||reg||1
